IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Social Security (Administration) Act 1999 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the claimant meets: whether I must claim
-- (s 11) and may claim from where I am (ss 29-31A); the day my claim is taken to be made when I contacted the Department first
-- (s 13); my start day (Schedule 2 clauses 3, 4, 5); when an undecided claim is taken to be refused (s 39); an advance for severe
-- financial hardship (s 51); what I must tell the Department and by when (ss 66A, 72, 74); the participation payment compliance
-- framework (Part 3 Division 3AA: ss 42AC-42AE failures, 42AL-42AM suspension and reconnection, 42AO-42AP preclusion and
-- cancellation); the day an adverse decision takes effect (s 118); and review (ss 109, 126-131, 142, 144, 147).
--
-- SEAT: the claimant -- the person who claims, receives or has received a social security payment (and the jobseeker under
-- mutual obligations). "How do I claim, and from when am I paid? What must I tell Services Australia, and by when? When can my
-- payment be suspended or cancelled, and from what day? How do I ask for a review, and how far back will a win go?" What the
-- Secretary decides is asked as a fact ("if the Secretary is satisfied that ...").
--
-- READ WITH the Social Security Act 1991 baseline (../../../social-security-act-1991/encodings/baseline-2026-10/), which
-- answers qualification, payability and rates (age pension, DSP, jobseeker payment, youth allowance, carer payments,
-- compensation). Whether I am "qualified" on a day is asked here as a fact, answered there. Cross-folder IMPORT is not possible
-- in the stable l4; NOTES.md names the link.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 163, compilation date 5 December 2025, includes amendments up to Act No. 73, 2025 (register id
-- C2026C00010, in 2 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00580.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The special payments and their claims (ss 12-12K, 17-27B, 46-50A, 59); employment pathway plans (Division 2A:
-- their content and exemptions) except as a source of requirements; Division 3A (declared program participants); payment
-- mechanics (ss 43-62) beyond s 51; the s 63 attendance and proof-of-life rules beyond what Division 3AA uses; tax file numbers
-- (ss 75-77); the automatic cancellations, suspensions and rate reductions of Part 3 Divisions 7-8 (ss 90-106B); concession
-- cards beyond s 11; nominees (Part 3A); income management (Parts 3AA, 3B); schooling requirements (Part 3C); information
-- gathering, confidentiality, offences and machinery (Parts 5-7). Debts are in the 1991 Act (Chapter 5), not this one.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the claimant's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Social Security (Administration) Act 1999 -- the claimant's questions`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the start day of a jobseeker payment or youth allowance claimant required to attend an interview is worked out under Schedule 2 clause 4A, which is not encoded`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `s 11 -- must I make a claim`

-- s 11(1): "a person who wants to be granted: (a) a social security payment; or (b) a concession card; must make a claim for the
-- payment or card in accordance with this Division." (2): not for a concession card for which the person is qualified under
-- Division 1 of Part 2A.1 of the 1991 Act (the pensioner concession card that comes with a pension) or Subdivision A of Division 3
-- (the automatic issue health care card); (3): not for a seniors health card the Secretary must issue under s 1061ZJA(3)-(5).
-- Subdivision B (ss 12-12K) deems claims for some special payments (not encoded). s 16: a claim is made by lodging a written
-- claim in the approved form or in a manner the Secretary approves (for example online).
DECLARE `What I want` IS ONE OF
    `a social security payment`
    `a concession card that comes automatically with my pension or payment (1991 Act Part 2A.1 Division 1 or Division 3 Subdivision A)`
    `a seniors health card the Secretary must issue to me under s 1061ZJA(3)-(5) of the 1991 Act`
    `another concession card`

@export Do I have to make a claim to get a social security payment or concession card (s 11)?
GIVEN `what I want` IS A `What I want` @desc What you want: a social security payment, a concession card that comes automatically with your pension or payment, a seniors health card the Secretary must reissue to you, or another concession card
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I make a claim` IF
    CONSIDER `what I want`
    WHEN `a concession card that comes automatically with my pension or payment (1991 Act Part 2A.1 Division 1 or Division 3 Subdivision A)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a seniors health card the Secretary must issue to me under s 1061ZJA(3)-(5) of the 1991 Act` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `ss 29-31A -- can I claim from where I am`

-- s 29(1): "a claim for a social security payment or a concession card may only be made by a person who: (a) is an Australian
-- resident; and (b) is in Australia." (2): a claim made when not resident or not in Australia "is taken not to have been made".
-- s 30: a claim for special benefit only by a person who "(a) is in Australia; and (b)" is an Australian resident or holds a visa
-- in a class the Minister determines. ss 30A, 31, 31A: exceptions (crisis payment visa holders, AGDRP, AVTOP, Disaster Recovery
-- Allowance, parenting payment within 13 weeks of an income support payment ending abroad, double orphan pension, special
-- category visa holders) -- asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Which payment I claim` IS ONE OF
    `special benefit`
    `another social security payment or a concession card`

@export Can I make a claim for a social security payment while I am where I am now (ss 29, 30)?
GIVEN `which` IS A `Which payment I claim` @desc Whether you are claiming special benefit, or another payment or a concession card
      `I am an Australian resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian resident within the meaning of the 1991 Act
      `I am in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Australia when you make the claim
      `I hold a visa the Minister has determined for special benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For special benefit: whether you hold a visa in a class the Minister has determined for s 729(2)(f)(v) of the 1991 Act
      `an exception in ss 30A, 31 or 31A applies to my claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the exceptions applies (crisis payment for some visa holders, disaster or terrorism payments, parenting payment within 13 weeks after an overseas income support payment ended, double orphan pension, or a New Zealand special category visa holder living here)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I claim from where I am` IF
    CONSIDER `which`
    WHEN `special benefit` THEN
        `I am in Australia` AND (`I am an Australian resident` OR `I hold a visa the Minister has determined for special benefit`)
    OTHERWISE
        `an exception in ss 30A, 31 or 31A applies to my claim` OR (`I am an Australian resident` AND `I am in Australia`)

§§ `s 13 -- the day my claim is taken to be made`

-- s 13(1): if "(a) the Department is contacted by or on behalf of a person in relation to a claim for a social security payment;
-- and (aa) the person is, on the day on which the Department is contacted, included in a class of persons determined in an
-- instrument under section 14A; and (b) the person is, on [that day], qualified for the social security payment; and (d) the
-- person lodges a claim ... within 14 days after the Department is contacted; the person is taken to have made a claim ... on the
-- day on which the Department was contacted." (2), (3), (3A): the same if the claim is lodged "more than 14 days, but not more than
-- 13 weeks, after" and the Secretary is satisfied that, throughout, (2) "the person was suffering from a medical condition" that
-- had "a significant adverse effect on the person's ability to lodge the claim earlier", or (3) the person was caring for, or the
-- partner of, someone with such a condition, or (3A) "in the special circumstances of the case, it was not reasonably practicable
-- for the person to lodge the claim earlier". (2) and (3) do not apply to crisis payment or special employment advance. The
-- s 14A class instrument is not deposited (a fact). 14 days after day C is C plus 14; 13 weeks is 91 days.
DECLARE `Why I lodged late` IS ONE OF
    `I had a medical condition that significantly hindered me`
    `I was caring for, or the partner of, someone whose medical condition significantly hindered me`
    `special circumstances made it not reasonably practicable to lodge earlier`
    `none of these`

@export I contacted Services Australia before lodging my claim. On what day is my claim taken to have been made (s 13)?
GIVEN `the day I contacted the Department` IS A DATE @desc The day you (or someone for you) first contacted the Department about the claim, by phone, online, post or in person
      `the day I lodged the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you actually lodged the claim
      `I was in the s 14A class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of contact, you were in a class of persons the Secretary's s 14A instrument determines
      `I was qualified on the day of contact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day of contact, you were already qualified for the payment
      `it is crisis payment or special employment advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is for crisis payment or a special employment advance
      `why late` IS A `Why I lodged late` @desc If you lodged more than 14 days after contact: the reason the Secretary is satisfied delayed you throughout, if any
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day is my claim taken to be made` MEANS
    IF `I was in the s 14A class` AND `I was qualified on the day of contact`
    THEN IF `the day I lodged the claim` AT MOST (`the day I contacted the Department` PLUS 14)
         THEN `the day I contacted the Department`
         ELSE IF `the day I lodged the claim` AT MOST (`the day I contacted the Department` PLUS 91) AND `a late reason the section accepts`
              THEN `the day I contacted the Department`
              ELSE `the day I lodged the claim`
    ELSE `the day I lodged the claim`
    WHERE
        `a late reason the section accepts` MEANS
            CONSIDER `why late`
            WHEN `I had a medical condition that significantly hindered me` THEN (NOT `it is crisis payment or special employment advance`)
            WHEN `I was caring for, or the partner of, someone whose medical condition significantly hindered me` THEN (NOT `it is crisis payment or special employment advance`)
            WHEN `special circumstances made it not reasonably practicable to lodge earlier` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE

§§ `Schedule 2 clauses 3, 4, 5 -- from what day am I paid`

-- cl 3(1): if "the person is qualified for the payment on the day on which the claim is made; the person's start day ... is the
-- day on which the claim is made" (cl 4A applies instead to some jobseeker and youth allowance claimants who must attend an
-- interview: not encoded). cl 4(1): if the person is not qualified on that day but "will, because of the passage of time or the
-- occurrence of an event, become qualified ... within the period of 13 weeks after the day on which the claim is made; and (d) the
-- person becomes so qualified within that period; the claim is taken to be made on the first day on which the person is qualified".
-- (2): every payment but special benefit is a "relevant social security payment", and parenting payment is not, for a person
-- qualified "because of the birth of a child". (6): a jobseeker or youth allowance claimant serving a liquid assets test waiting
-- period is taken to claim on the first day qualified. cl 5(1): if on the start day the person "is subject to one or more
-- exclusion periods" (a waiting period, a non-payment period, a compensation preclusion period, gaol ...), the start day is "the
-- first day after the end of that period" (all of them). The claim day is the s 13 day where s 13 applies.
DECLARE `My start day` IS ONE OF
    `my start day is` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `no start day: I was not qualified on the claim day and did not become qualified within 13 weeks after it, so the claim cannot be granted on these facts`

@export From what day will my social security payment start (Schedule 2, clauses 3, 4 and 5)?
GIVEN `the claim day` IS A DATE @desc The day your claim is made (or taken to be made under s 13)
      `I am qualified on the claim day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are qualified for the payment on the claim day (see the Social Security Act 1991 baseline)
      `the day I become qualified` IS A DATE @desc If not qualified on the claim day: the first day you become qualified (ignored otherwise)
      `it is special benefit, or parenting payment because of a birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment is special benefit, or parenting payment you qualify for because of a child's birth (these cannot be claimed early)
      `I am serving a liquid assets waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For jobseeker payment or youth allowance: whether you are serving a liquid assets test waiting period when you claim
      `I am subject to an exclusion period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the day that would be your start day, you are subject to an exclusion period (a waiting period, non-payment period, compensation preclusion period, or time in gaol)
      `the last day of my exclusion periods` IS A DATE @desc If so: the last day of the last of those periods (ignored otherwise)
      `I must attend an interview for jobseeker or youth allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim jobseeker payment or youth allowance and are required to attend an interview, so that clause 4A applies
GIVETH AN `Answer` `My start day`
`From what day will my payment start` MEANS
    IF `I must attend an interview for jobseeker or youth allowance`
    THEN `not covered` `the start day of a jobseeker payment or youth allowance claimant required to attend an interview is worked out under Schedule 2 clause 4A, which is not encoded`
    ELSE IF `I am qualified on the claim day`
         THEN `answered` (`my start day is` (`after exclusions` `the claim day`))
         ELSE IF     `I am serving a liquid assets waiting period`
                  OR (    (NOT `it is special benefit, or parenting payment because of a birth`)
                      AND `the day I become qualified` AT MOST (`the claim day` PLUS 91))
              THEN `answered` (`my start day is` (`after exclusions` `the day I become qualified`))
              ELSE `answered` `no start day: I was not qualified on the claim day and did not become qualified within 13 weeks after it, so the claim cannot be granted on these facts`
    WHERE
        `after exclusions` d MEANS
            IF `I am subject to an exclusion period` AND `the last day of my exclusion periods` AT LEAST d
            THEN `the last day of my exclusion periods` PLUS 1
            ELSE d

§§ `s 39 -- my claim has not been decided`

-- s 39(1): "if the Secretary does not make a determination regarding a claim within the period of 13 weeks after the day on which
-- the claim was made, the Secretary is taken to have made, at the end of that period, a determination rejecting the claim."
-- (4): the days from the Secretary asking for information to its being given "[are] not counted". (5): for a s 13 claim the 13
-- weeks run from the day of the actual claim. (3): for an early claim (Schedule 2 cl 4) they run from the day the person becomes
-- qualified. The deemed rejection is a decision I can seek review of (s 129(5)). The end of 13 weeks after day D is D plus 91;
-- each day not counted adds a day.
@export My claim has not been decided. On what day is it taken to have been rejected (s 39)?
GIVEN `the day the 13 weeks run from` IS A DATE @desc The day you actually lodged the claim (or, for a claim made early, the day you became qualified)
      `days waiting for information I was asked for` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days from when the Secretary asked for information about the claim to when it was given (these days are not counted)
GIVETH A DATE
`On what day is my undecided claim taken to be rejected` MEANS
    `the day the 13 weeks run from` PLUS (91 PLUS `days waiting for information I was asked for`)

§§ `s 51 -- an advance if I would suffer severe financial hardship`

-- s 51(1): if a claim for a benefit or pension by a person in Australia is granted (or payment resumes under s 85), and "the
-- Secretary is satisfied that, if the person is required to wait until the end of ... the first instalment period ... the person
-- will suffer severe financial hardship; the Secretary may determine that a specified amount is to be paid to the person in
-- advance." (4): it "is not to exceed the amount that, in the opinion of the Secretary, would be the total of the amounts payable
-- to the person for the first 14 days on which the benefit or pension is payable". (5): it is an advance of those instalments.
@export My claim for a pension or benefit has been granted and waiting for the first payment would cause me severe hardship. What is the most I can be advanced (s 51)?
GIVEN `my claim is granted or my payment resumed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your claim for a benefit or pension has been granted (or payment resumed after cancellation or suspension), and you are in Australia
      `the Secretary is satisfied of severe financial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is satisfied you would suffer severe financial hardship waiting for the first instalment
      `my payment for the first 14 days` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of what your payment would be for the first 14 days it is payable, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be advanced` MEANS
    IF `my claim is granted or my payment resumed` AND `the Secretary is satisfied of severe financial hardship`
    THEN `my payment for the first 14 days`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 66A, 72, 74 -- what I must tell the Department, and by when`

-- s 66A(1)-(3): a person who has claimed (granted or undecided), is being paid, or has been paid, must "within 14 days after the day
-- on which the event or change occurs, inform the Department" of an event or change that "might affect the payment". s 72(3): the
-- period a notice under ss 67-69 specifies is "(a) ... receipt by the person of a compensation payment--... 7 days after the day on
-- which the person becomes aware that he or she has received, or is to receive, a compensation payment"; "(b) ... any other
-- information ... 14 days after: (i) the day on which the event or change of circumstances occurs; or (ii) the day on which the
-- person becomes aware that the event or change ... is likely to occur"; (6): "the death of a person ... 28 days after the day on
-- which the event occurs". (4): in special circumstances the Secretary may direct a longer period. s 74: failing to comply with a
-- notice is an offence, "Imprisonment for 6 months", "only to the extent to which the person is capable of complying".
DECLARE `What I must report` IS ONE OF
    `a change of circumstances that might affect my payment (s 66A)`
    `under a notice: that I have received, or will receive, a compensation payment`
    `under a notice: the death of a person the notice names`
    `under a notice: another event or change the notice names`

@export Something has changed. By when must I tell Services Australia (ss 66A, 72)?
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I must report` @desc What you must report: a change that might affect your payment (the general duty), or, under a notice you were given, a compensation payment, a death, or another event the notice names
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day the change or event happened (for compensation: the day you became aware you have received or will receive it)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I tell the Department` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `under a notice: that I have received, or will receive, a compensation payment` THEN `the day` PLUS 7
    WHEN `under a notice: the death of a person the notice names` THEN `the day` PLUS 28
    OTHERWISE `the day` PLUS 14

§§ `Part 3 Division 3AA -- mutual obligation, work refusal and unemployment failures`

-- (Situation: I receive, or have claimed, a participation payment -- jobseeker payment, youth allowance (not as a full-time
-- student or new apprentice), parenting payment for some parents, special benefit for a nominated visa holder (Sch 1) -- and I am
-- not a declared program participant (s 42AB).)
-- s 42AC(1): "A person commits a mutual obligation failure if the person is receiving a participation payment and any of the
-- following applies: (a) the person fails to comply with a requirement that was notified ... under subsection 63(2) or (4); (b) ...
-- fails to comply with a requirement, under section 40A, to enter into an employment pathway plan; (c) ... fails to attend, or to be
-- punctual for, an appointment ...; (d) ... fails to attend, to be punctual for, or to participate in, an activity ... [in] an
-- employment pathway plan ...; (e) ... fails to satisfy the Secretary that the person has undertaken adequate job search efforts
-- ...; (f) ... fails to comply with any other requirement of the plan ...; (g) the Secretary is satisfied that the person acted in
-- an inappropriate manner [at an appointment or activity]; (h) the person intentionally acts in a manner and it is reasonably
-- foreseeable that acting in that manner could result in an offer of paid work ... not being made ...; (i) the person fails to: (i)
-- attend a job interview; or (ii) act on a job opportunity when requested". (1A): no failure in not accepting, or not doing, paid
-- work "of more than 15 hours per week" if "the person is the principal carer of at least one child or has a partial capacity to
-- work".
DECLARE `What I did or did not do` IS ONE OF
    `I did not comply with a requirement in a s 63 notice`
    `I did not enter into an employment pathway plan when required`
    `I missed, or was late for, an appointment`
    `I missed, was late for, or did not take part in, an activity in my plan`
    `I did not satisfy the Secretary of adequate job search`
    `I did not comply with another requirement of my plan`
    `the Secretary is satisfied I behaved inappropriately at an appointment or activity`
    `I intentionally acted so that a job offer would foreseeably not be made`
    `I did not attend a job interview, or act on a job opportunity, when asked`
    `I did not accept an offer of paid work, or do paid work`

@export Have I committed a "mutual obligation failure" on my jobseeker or other participation payment (s 42AC)?
GIVEN `I receive a participation payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving a participation payment (jobseeker payment, youth allowance other than as a full-time student or apprentice, parenting payment with mutual obligations, or special benefit as a nominated visa holder)
      `what` IS A `What I did or did not do` @desc What happened
      `I am a principal carer or have partial capacity to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the principal carer of at least one child, or have a partial capacity to work
      `the work was more than 15 hours a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it concerns paid work: whether the work was more than 15 hours a week
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed a mutual obligation failure` IF
        `I receive a participation payment`
    AND (NOT (    `what` EQUALS `I did not accept an offer of paid work, or do paid work`
              AND `I am a principal carer or have partial capacity to work`
              AND `the work was more than 15 hours a week`))

-- s 42AD(1): a work refusal failure if the person "(a) is receiving a participation payment; and ... (b) ... refuses or fails to
-- accept an offer of paid work in Australia, except particular paid work that is unsuitable to be done by the person" (Division
-- 2B, s 40X, as a fact). (2): not if a principal carer or partial capacity and the offer was of "more than 15 hours per week".
@export I turned down a job offer while on a participation payment. Is that a "work refusal failure" (s 42AD)?
GIVEN `I receive a participation payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving a participation payment
      `I refused or did not accept an offer of paid work in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you refused, or failed to accept, an offer of paid work in Australia
      `the work was unsuitable for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that particular work was unsuitable for you under s 40X (for example because of your health, caring duties, or pay and conditions below the law)
      `I am a principal carer or have partial capacity to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the principal carer of at least one child, or have a partial capacity to work
      `the work was more than 15 hours a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offered work was more than 15 hours a week
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed a work refusal failure` IF
        `I receive a participation payment`
    AND `I refused or did not accept an offer of paid work in Australia`
    AND (NOT `the work was unsuitable for me`)
    AND (NOT (`I am a principal carer or have partial capacity to work` AND `the work was more than 15 hours a week`))

-- s 42AE(1), (2): an unemployment failure if the person is receiving, or has claimed, a participation payment and "becomes
-- unemployed: (i) as a direct or indirect result of a voluntary act of the person; or (ii) as a result of the person's misconduct
-- as an employee." (3): not for a voluntary act "if the person satisfies the Secretary that the voluntary act was reasonable". (4):
-- not if a principal carer or partial capacity and the work was "of more than 15 hours per week".
DECLARE `How I became unemployed` IS ONE OF
    `I left the job voluntarily`
    `I was dismissed for misconduct`
    `for another reason (for example redundancy, or the job ended)`

@export I left my job or was dismissed. Is that an "unemployment failure" for my participation payment (s 42AE)?
GIVEN `I receive or have claimed a participation payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving, or have claimed, a participation payment
      `how` IS A `How I became unemployed` @desc How you became unemployed
      `the Secretary accepts it was reasonable to leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you left voluntarily: whether you have satisfied the Secretary that leaving was reasonable
      `I am a principal carer or have partial capacity to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the principal carer of at least one child, or have a partial capacity to work
      `the work was more than 15 hours a week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the job was more than 15 hours a week
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I committed an unemployment failure` IF
        `I receive or have claimed a participation payment`
    AND (NOT (`I am a principal carer or have partial capacity to work` AND `the work was more than 15 hours a week`))
    AND (    (`how` EQUALS `I left the job voluntarily` AND (NOT `the Secretary accepts it was reasonable to leave`))
          OR `how` EQUALS `I was dismissed for misconduct`)

-- s 42AF(1), 42AG(1)(a): for a mutual obligation or work refusal failure the Secretary "may" determine the payment is not payable
-- for a payment suspension period. s 42AM(1): the Secretary "must impose a requirement (the reconnection requirement)" and notify
-- it; (3), (4): the payment is cancelled "at the end of the 4 weeks" if the person "fails to comply with the reconnection
-- requirement within 4 weeks after it is notified" (unless the Secretary chose an earlier end). s 42AL(3), (4): the suspension
-- ends immediately before the day of compliance, and the payment "is taken to be payable ... from the start of that period" (back
-- pay, which a s 42AN reduction may cut). s 42AF(2): for persistent failures with no reasonable excuse the Secretary may also
-- reduce an instalment by half or all of it (s 42AN), or cancel (s 42AP). 4 weeks after notification on day N ends on N plus 28.
DECLARE `My payment after a suspension` IS ONE OF
    `suspended until I meet the reconnection requirement; once I do, it is payable again back to the start of the suspension (back pay), less any s 42AN reduction (s 42AL)`
    `cancelled at the end of the 4 weeks after I was told of the reconnection requirement, because I did not meet it in time (s 42AM(3), (4)); the 4 weeks ended on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `the suspension ended on the earlier day the Secretary chose; the payment is payable back to the start of the suspension (s 42AL(3)(b), (4))`

@export My participation payment was suspended for a mutual obligation or work refusal failure. What happens if I reconnect, or don't (ss 42AL, 42AM)?
GIVEN `the day I was told of the reconnection requirement` IS A DATE @desc The day the Secretary notified you of the reconnection requirement (for example to attend an appointment)
      `the day I met it` IS A DATE @desc The day you complied with the reconnection requirement (ignored if you have not)
      `I have met it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have complied with the reconnection requirement
      `the Secretary chose an earlier end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary determined that the suspension should end on an earlier day
GIVETH A `My payment after a suspension`
`What happens to my suspended payment` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary chose an earlier end`
    THEN `the suspension ended on the earlier day the Secretary chose; the payment is payable back to the start of the suspension (s 42AL(3)(b), (4))`
    ELSE IF `I have met it` AND `the day I met it` AT MOST (`the day I was told of the reconnection requirement` PLUS 28)
         THEN `suspended until I meet the reconnection requirement; once I do, it is payable again back to the start of the suspension (back pay), less any s 42AN reduction (s 42AL)`
         ELSE `cancelled at the end of the 4 weeks after I was told of the reconnection requirement, because I did not meet it in time (s 42AM(3), (4)); the 4 weeks ended on` (`the day I was told of the reconnection requirement` PLUS 28)

-- s 42AO(1): for a claimant, "participation payments are not payable ... for the period (the unemployment preclusion period) of:
-- (a) 4 weeks beginning on the day the person becomes unemployed ...; or (b) 6 weeks beginning on that day, if, during the 6 months
-- ending on the day immediately before that day, relocation assistance, for the employment ..., has been paid". s 42AP(3), (5): for
-- a recipient the payment "is cancelled at the start of the following day (the cancellation day): (a) the day that the person
-- becomes unemployed" (or (b) a later instalment period the Secretary prefers), and no participation payment is payable for "4
-- weeks beginning on the cancellation day", or 6 with relocation assistance. Reading (NOTES.md finding 7): "the following day"
-- introduces the list, so the cancellation day is the day of unemployment. A period of 4 weeks beginning on day X ends on X plus
-- 27; payment can start again on X plus 28 (plus 42 for 6 weeks). Both are exclusion periods for a new claim's start day
-- (Schedule 2 cl 5(1B)).
@export After an unemployment failure, from what day can a participation payment be paid to me again (ss 42AO, 42AP)?
GIVEN `the day I became unemployed` IS A DATE @desc The day you became unemployed through your voluntary act or misconduct
      `I was paid relocation assistance for that job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Commonwealth relocation assistance (a payment the Secretary has specified) was paid to you or for you, for that job, in the 6 months before you became unemployed
      `the Secretary chose a later cancellation day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were receiving the payment: whether the Secretary decided to cancel from a later instalment period instead
      `the later cancellation day` IS A DATE @desc That later day, the first day of the first instalment period after the Secretary's determination (ignored otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day can I be paid again after an unemployment failure` MEANS
    `the start` PLUS `the length`
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS
            IF `the Secretary chose a later cancellation day` THEN `the later cancellation day` ELSE `the day I became unemployed`
        `the length` MEANS
            IF `I was paid relocation assistance for that job` THEN 42 ELSE 28

§§ `s 118 -- from what day does a decision against me take effect`

-- (Situation: my payment has been reduced, suspended or cancelled.)
-- s 118(2): if "an adverse determination is made following a person having informed the Department of the occurrence of an event
-- or change of circumstances; and (b) the person is not paid an instalment ... after the occurrence of the event or change and
-- before the determination is made; the determination takes effect on the day on which the event or change of circumstances
-- occurred." (5): after "a statement about a matter in accordance with a notice under section 67 or 68, the determination takes
-- effect on the day on which the matter arose." (7): if my contravention of the Act "causes a delay in the making of the
-- determination", and (8), (9) if a "false statement or misrepresentation" caused payment, it "takes effect on such day (which may
-- be earlier than the day on which the determination is made) as is specified in the determination". (11): a payment suspended and
-- then cancelled under s 80, 81 or 82 is cancelled from "the day on which the payment was suspended". (13): "In any other case ...
-- on the day on which it is made; or ... if a later day is specified in the determination, on that day." The special rules in
-- (2A), (2B), (2D), (2E), (3), (4), (5A), (5B), (12)-(12D) are not encoded.
DECLARE `How the decision came about` IS ONE OF
    `after I told the Department of a change, and no instalment was paid to me after the change and before the decision`
    `after I gave a statement in response to a notice under s 67 or s 68`
    `my false statement or misrepresentation, or my breach of the Act that delayed the decision`
    `my payment was suspended under s 80, 81 or 82 and is now cancelled`
    `any other way`

@export A decision has reduced, suspended or cancelled my payment. From what day does it take effect (s 118)?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How the decision came about` @desc How the adverse decision came about
      `the day of the change or matter` IS A DATE @desc The day the change of circumstances occurred, or the matter in your statement arose
      `the day specified in the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision itself specifies (for a false statement or a delay you caused; or a later day, if any, in any other case)
      `a later day is specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In any other case: whether the decision specifies a later day than the day it was made
      `the day the decision was made` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision was made
      `the day my payment was suspended` IS A DATE @desc For a cancellation after a suspension: the day the payment was suspended (ignored otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day does the decision against me take effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `after I told the Department of a change, and no instalment was paid to me after the change and before the decision` THEN `the day of the change or matter`
    WHEN `after I gave a statement in response to a notice under s 67 or s 68` THEN `the day of the change or matter`
    WHEN `my false statement or misrepresentation, or my breach of the Act that delayed the decision` THEN `the day specified in the decision`
    WHEN `my payment was suspended under s 80, 81 or 82 and is now cancelled` THEN `the day my payment was suspended`
    WHEN `any other way` THEN
        IF `a later day is specified` THEN `the day specified in the decision` ELSE `the day the decision was made`

§§ `ss 126-131, 142, 144, 147 -- getting a decision reviewed`

-- s 129(1): "a person affected by a decision of an officer under the social security law may apply to the Secretary for review"
-- (a deemed decision included, (5)); (3): for pension bonus and essential medical equipment payment, not "more than 13 weeks after
-- the giving of the notice"; (4)(a): not for "a decision made by the Secretary himself or herself". s 135: the review must be done.
-- s 142(1): the ART may review "(a) a decision of the Secretary, the Chief Executive Centrelink or an authorised review officer
-- made under section 126 or 135; or (b) a decision under this Act made personally by the Secretary or the Chief Executive
-- Centrelink". s 147(1) item 1: the ART Act's time limit (s 18) "does not apply". s 144: the ART cannot review, among others, a
-- decision "(f) under section 16" (form and manner of claim), "(faa) under subsection 42AM(1)" (imposing a reconnection
-- requirement), "(k) to give a notice under Subdivision B of Division 6 of Part 3" (the information notices of ss 66A-74),
-- "(m) under section 131 or 145" (continuing payment pending review).
DECLARE `The decision I want reviewed` IS ONE OF
    `an officer's decision about my payment, claim or card`
    `an officer's decision about my pension bonus or essential medical equipment payment`
    `a decision made personally by the Secretary or the Chief Executive Centrelink`
    `a decision about the form or manner of my claim (s 16)`
    `a decision to impose a reconnection requirement on me (s 42AM(1))`
    `a decision to give me an information notice`
    `a decision whether my payment continues while my review is decided (s 131 or s 145)`

DECLARE `How I can have it reviewed` IS ONE OF
    `ask for internal review by the Secretary (s 129, no time limit), then apply to the ART (s 142, no time limit, s 147)`
    `ask for internal review within 13 weeks after notice of the decision (s 129(3)), then apply to the ART (s 142)`
    `apply directly to the ART (s 142(1)(b), no time limit, s 147)`
    `ask for internal review (s 129, no time limit); the ART cannot review this decision (s 144)`

@export How can I get a Centrelink decision under the social security law reviewed (ss 129, 142, 144)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision I want reviewed` @desc Which decision you want reviewed
GIVETH A `How I can have it reviewed`
`How can I have the decision reviewed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `an officer's decision about my payment, claim or card` THEN `ask for internal review by the Secretary (s 129, no time limit), then apply to the ART (s 142, no time limit, s 147)`
    WHEN `an officer's decision about my pension bonus or essential medical equipment payment` THEN `ask for internal review within 13 weeks after notice of the decision (s 129(3)), then apply to the ART (s 142)`
    WHEN `a decision made personally by the Secretary or the Chief Executive Centrelink` THEN `apply directly to the ART (s 142(1)(b), no time limit, s 147)`
    OTHERWISE `ask for internal review (s 129, no time limit); the ART cannot review this decision (s 144)`

-- s 109(1): if I apply for review "within 13 weeks after the notice is given" and win, "the favourable determination takes effect
-- on the day on which the determination embodying the original decision took effect"; (2): if "more than 13 weeks after", it takes
-- effect "on the day on which the application for review was made"; (3): if I was never given notice, from the original day. s 147
-- item 8: the same 13-week rule for a win at the ART when the first review application was more than 13 weeks after notice.
-- "within 13 weeks after" day N: on or before N plus 91.
@export If my review succeeds, from what day will the better decision take effect (s 109)?
GIVEN `I was given notice of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were given notice of the original decision
      `the day of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice of the original decision was given to you (ignored if none)
      `the day I applied for review` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied to the Secretary for review
      `the day the original decision took effect` IS A DATE @desc The day the original (adverse) decision took effect
GIVETH A DATE
`From what day will a successful review take effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `I was given notice of the decision`) OR `the day I applied for review` AT MOST (`the day of the notice` PLUS 91)
    THEN `the day the original decision took effect`
    ELSE `the day I applied for review`

-- s 131(1): if "(a) an adverse decision is made ...; and (aa) [it] is not made under Division 3AA of Part 3 ...; and (b) [it]: (i)
-- depends on the exercise of a discretion, or the holding of an opinion, by a person; or (ii) would result in the application of a
-- compliance penalty period; and (c) a person applies to the Secretary under section 129 for review ...; the Secretary may declare
-- that the payment ... is to continue pending the determination of the review". A discretion, answered conditionally; the ART
-- cannot review the decision on it (s 144(m)).
DECLARE `Can my payment continue during review` IS ONE OF
    `the Secretary may declare that my payment continues until the review is decided, as if the decision had not been made (s 131); this is the Secretary's discretion and the ART cannot review it`
    `s 131 does not allow my payment to continue during the review`

@export I have asked for review of a decision cutting my payment. Can my payment keep going until the review is decided (s 131)?
GIVEN `I applied for internal review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have applied to the Secretary for review under s 129
      `it is a mutual obligation compliance decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was made under Part 3 Division 3AA (mutual obligation, work refusal or unemployment failures)
      `it turns on a discretion or opinion, or applies a compliance penalty period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision depends on someone's discretion or opinion, or would apply a compliance penalty period
GIVETH A `Can my payment continue during review`
`Can my payment continue during review (s 131)` MEANS
    IF `I applied for internal review` AND (NOT `it is a mutual obligation compliance decision`) AND `it turns on a discretion or opinion, or applies a compliance penalty period`
    THEN `the Secretary may declare that my payment continues until the review is decided, as if the decision had not been made (s 131); this is the Secretary's discretion and the ART cannot review it`
    ELSE `s 131 does not allow my payment to continue during the review`
